        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(terminal-core): prevent String.replace $ pattern injection in display-string",
        "body": "fix(terminal-core): prevent String.replace $ pattern injection in display-string\n\n## Description\n\n`String.prototype.replace()` with a string second argument interprets `$` sequences as special replacement patterns (`$&`, `` $` ``, `$'`, `$1`-`$9`, `$<name>`). When the user's home directory path contains such characters (e.g. `/home/$&data`), the replacement produces a corrupted display path.\n\n## Fix\n\nUsing a replacer function `() => fallbackHome` instead of the raw string argument prevents `$` pattern interpretation, ensuring the literal home directory path is used regardless of its content.\n\n## Real module test evidence (vitest, 2/2 passed)\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  2 passed (2)\n```\n\n```\n ✓ displayString > shortens whole-value homes and child paths without clipping sibling prefixes\n ✓ displayString > uses OPENCLAW_HOME as the display prefix\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/replace-home-dollar-injection",
